TITLE:: RLTableGroup
summary:: A finite group given by its table: the roots of an extension when they do not commute
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLExtension, Classes/RLCategory, Classes/RLWreath, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
The elements are the places code::0 .. size - 1::, 0 the identity; code::table[a][b]:: is the product a b. The group answers what link::Classes/RLExtension:: asks of the roots (code::pcZero::, code::pcAdd::, code::pcNeg::...: the "sum" is the product, in that order), so a group of transformations can be the roots of a larger group. An automorphism is the list of the images of the elements, in their order.

code::
~ti = RLTableGroup.of(RLRelationContext.pitchClasses(RLEDO(12)).category);     // T and I on 12 notes
~ti.size;  ~ti.isAbelian;                 // 24, false
~ti.automorphisms.size;                   // 48
~ti.center.collect { |a| ~ti.name(a) };   // the identity and the tritone

RLTableGroup.dihedral(4).orders;          // [[1, 1], [2, 5], [4, 2]]
RLTableGroup.quaternion.automorphisms.size;       // 24

// T and I of 24 quarter-tones as T and I of 12 notes by two types
~d = RLTableGroup.dihedral(12);           // r^i is T_i, s r^i is I_-i
~quarter = Array.series(12) ++ Array.fill(12) { |i| 12 + ((i - 1) % 12) };     // every inversion moved by one
~ext = RLExtension.general(~d, [[0, 1], [1, 0]], [~d.pcs, ~quarter], [[0, 0], [0, 1]]);
~ext.orders == RLTableGroup.dihedral(24).orders;          // true
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: table
The products: code::table[a][b]:: is a b. Refused when it is no group's table with its identity first.
argument:: names
A name for each element, for printing (their places when nil).

METHOD:: cyclic
METHOD:: dihedral
METHOD:: quaternion
The cyclic group of n elements; the dihedral group of 2n (code::r^i:: is i, code::s r^i:: is n + i); the quaternion group (1, -1, i, -i, j, -j, k, -k).

METHOD:: of
The group an link::Classes/RLCategory:: is, when it is one: its arrows in their order, the identity moved to the front, each named by its word.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: table
METHOD:: names
METHOD:: name
METHOD:: size
METHOD:: pcs
The table; the names; the name of an element; how many elements; their places.

METHOD:: mul
METHOD:: inv
METHOD:: order
METHOD:: orders
METHOD:: isAbelian
METHOD:: center
The product and the inverse; the order of an element; how many elements have each order, as code::[order, count]:: pairs; whether the group commutes; the elements that commute with all.

METHOD:: inner
The automorphism x -> a x a^-1, as the list of the images.

METHOD:: isAutomorphism
Whether a list of images is one to one and keeps the products.

METHOD:: automorphisms
Every automorphism: the images of a few generators are tried among the elements of the same order, and each choice that extends to the whole table is kept.

METHOD:: generators
METHOD:: span
A few elements that generate the group, taken greedily; what a list of elements generates.

METHOD:: pcZero
METHOD:: pcAdd
METHOD:: pcNeg
METHOD:: pcSub
METHOD:: isFinite
What link::Classes/RLExtension:: asks of the roots: the identity, the product, the inverse.
